    <problem>
      <p>Second derivative of $$y = 4^{x} + x^{2}\text{sin}\mspace{2mu}(x)$$</p>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <p>$$4^{x}\left( {\text{ln}\mspace{2mu} 4} \right)^{2} + 2\mspace{2mu}\text{sin}\mspace{2mu} x + 4x\mspace{2mu}\text{cos}\mspace{2mu} x - x^{2}\text{sin}\mspace{2mu} x$$</p>
    </solution>
